<div class="guide-styles" data-ay-injected="true" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid Tank in Wrath of the Lich King Classic for Phase 4. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from Heroics, Honor, BoE craftables, and the new Raid loot added to Titan Rune Dungeons.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot-gear">Feral Druid Tank Best in Slot Gear, Gems, and Enchants - Pre-Raid Phase 4</h2>When planning out your character's pre-raid gearing in WotLK Classic, the first thing to note is that itemization for Ferals has been greatly simplified in WotLK compared to vanilla and TBC. All leather armor now follows a simple formula of providing two primary attributes, Agility and Stamina, and 2-3 secondary DPS stats at fixed ratios relative to the amount of Agility on the item. Likewise, all tanking accessories (cloaks, necklaces, and rings) also follow a simple formula of providing Stamina and Strength as primary attributes, and Expertise or avoidance stats as secondaries (also with set stat ratios). As a result, the total allocation of useful stats on any gear piece is entirely determined by its item level, and a new piece of gear with higher item level than your current piece will almost always be a tanking upgrade, regardless of the details of what stats are present on the two items. This means that, especially early on in your character's gear progression when you are flooded with gear options from dungeons, PvP rewards, and other sources, you really do not need to think too hard about what pieces to equip, and can use item level as an excellent proxy for tanking value when evaluating potential upgrades. When comparing two pieces with the <i>same</i> item level, then the one with higher Stamina on it will pretty much always be better for bear tanking.<br/>
<br/>Second, Ferals in WotLK will no longer to need to worry about optimizing for crit immunity in tanking sets. This is because the new version of the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33856/survival-of-the-fittest">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_enrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Survival of the Fittest</span></a> talent makes all bears uncrittable by raid bosses even without any gear equipped. As a result, Resilience Rating is now a worthless tanking stat for bears in PvE, and Defense Rating is only valuable for the avoidance it provides.<br/>
<br/>Finally, the value of avoidance stats, especially Agility, plummets in WotLK compared to TBC. This is because WotLK introduces a mechanic called <i>diminishing returns</i> on all avoidance stats in order to counteract a fundamental <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/tbc/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-overview-pve#strengths">scaling issue</a> with avoidance in prior expansions. In TBC, avoidance stats exhibited <i>increasing returns</i> in their value: each additional 1% Dodge provided more value for tank survival than the previous. This resulted in tanks (especially high avoidance tanks like Feral Druids) scaling far better with gear than desired, so much so that the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/tbc/spell=45769/sunwell-radiance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_circleofrenewal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sunwell Radiance</span></a> aura needed to be implemented so that mitigation gear would continue to be relevant for tanks at the end of the expansion. In WotLK, avoidance stats have been re-worked so that each point in Defense Rating, Dodge Rating, and Agility provides less of a % Dodge and % Miss increase than the previous in order to counteract this effect. As a result, Agility becomes much less efficient for improving tank survivability than Stamina, and even aggressively skewed tanking sets should prioritize Stamina gems moving forward.<br/>
<br/>Shown below is a recommended gear configuration that can be easily assembled by a Feral tank in Phase 4 prior to entering any WotLK raids. The set includes primarily items that can be farmed in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/news/wrath-classic-3-4-3-ptr-development-notes-9-7-wotlk-classic-334920">Titan Rune Gamma</a> dungeons, either directly from boss drops or indirectly via <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/news/wrath-classic-3-4-3-ptr-defilers-scourgestone-wotlk-classic-334787">Defiler's Scourgestone</a> accumulation. As a change from our pre-raid lists in prior phases, the recommended setup also includes a handful of easily obtainable PvP and BoE crafted gear. We felt that the inclusion of these items was reasonable even in a pre-raid list because (a) the two PvP items can be rapidly farmed in Battlegrounds without setting foot in competitive Arenas, and (b) the most expensive reagents for the three crafted items (<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49908/primordial-saronite">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_felflamebreath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordial Saronite</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47556/crusader-orb">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_rune.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Orb</span></a>) can be purchased using the farmable <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=2711/defilers-scourgestone">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Defiler's Scourgestone</span></span></a> currency from Titan Rune Gamma dungeons.<br/>
