<section class="gear-planner-navigation-summary">Summary</section>
<hr class="gear-planner-navigation-divider"/></section>
<section class="gear-planner-customization" data-currently-visible="false"></section>
<div class="gear-planner-slots-controls">
<div class="gear-planner-slots-controls-buttons">
<a class="btn btn-small gear-planner-button-container-link fa fa-link" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/gear-planner/druid/night-elf/BgFQFfUDIyEyMiAQNTEgMAMTUR8gNQAB8B8wMDFuZ3YxMW5ndDIxenB2MzFyZzI0MXJmejUxcmcxgUC8UwEI_wChpCCctwIAuAyDILxQAPOwAJy3hWC57wDG3QCctyCct0CctwZgtA8AnLcgnLdAnLeHYMLrAOylAJy3IJy3QJy3iEDC5wDW6ACctyCct4kAyKoA8zCKILxUAPkaAJy3CwC6cwwgsZ8AnLcNALfoDgC_3o8gsbgAujgAnMKQQKWXAPxDAJy3IJy3EgCxxQ" style="margin-left:5px;float:right">Link</a>
<button class="btn btn-small fa fa-user gear-planner-button-container-model">Toggle Model</button></div>
<div class="slider not-editable has-labels" data-track="progress">
<div class="slider-track">
<div class="slider-track-handle" style="left: 100%;"></div>
<div class="slider-track-bar">
<div class="slider-track-bar-progress" style="width: 100%;"></div></div></div>
<div class="slider-labels">
<span class="slider-labels-title">Level</span>
<span class="slider-labels-values">
<span class="slider-labels-values-sizer">80</span>
<input class="slider-labels-values-input" data-field-filled="true" disabled="" style="width: 20px;" type="text"/>
<span class="slider-labels-values-max">80</span></span></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<br/>Note that the above BiS setup includes the Engineering-exclusive enchants <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=63770/reticulated-armor-webbing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reticulated Armor Webbing</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67839/mind-amplification-dish">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mind Amplification Dish</span></a>. As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-overview-pve#best-professions">class overview guide</a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> is such an insanely overpowered profession for PvE that is assumed that any competitive Feral tank player will have it. In contrast, your second profession choice has hardly any impact in WotLK since all crafting professions provide very comparable PvE benefits, so no other profession-exclusive gear augmentations are assumed. <br/>
<br/>Also note that the BiS pre-raid setup is 2.88% below the Hit cap of 8% against a level 83 raid boss, and 2.97% below the Expertise cap of 14%. This is completely fine! As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-stat-priority-attributes-pve">Stats &amp; Attributes guide</a>, reaching the Hit and Expertise caps is <i>never</i> a gearing goal, and Hit /<wbr/> Expertise Rating simply have a quantifiable TPS value that can be compared to the value of other Threat stats like Attack Power or Haste Rating. In the pre-raid setup above, making gear swaps to gain more Hit Rating or Expertise Rating would result in an objectively worse gear set even if your attacks miss less often. Tank players in particular are often incorrectly driven to over-value Hit or Expertise in their gearing simply because missing your first <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48564/mangle-bear">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_mangle2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mangle (Bear)</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48480/maul">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_maul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maul</span></a> of a pull can <i>feel</i> really bad, especially when tanking for competitive DPS players. However, pretty much any case of unfavorable opening pull variance can be rectified simply by vocalizing the miss on comms, and by having a <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42641/global-thermal-sapper-charge">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_supersappercharge.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Global Thermal Sapper Charge</span></a> or other <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> explosive cooldown available for on-demand snap Threat. Both of these strategies will be <i>much</i> more efficient for improving the smoothness of your raid clears than sacrificing an excessive amount of survivability for the sake of Hit and Expertise caps.<br/>
<br/>Finally, it is worth clarifying that while the BiS pre-raid setups for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<span class="q10">Horde</span> and <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>
<span class="q3">Alliance</span> bears are identical, several of the items are named differently depending on your faction. The embedded configuration above uses <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>
<span class="q3">Alliance</span> names for these items, but the detailed item listings just below include both faction-specific names, so make sure to check those out if you are a <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<span class="q10">Horde</span> player.<div data-manual-placement-group="guide-body-article-au" style="margin: auto; display: flex; justify-content: center; min-height: 90px;">
<div id="guide-body-article-au__ayManagerEnv__1"></div></div>
